# What a deploy does not need.
#
# `src2/deploy/deploy.sh` names what a version is built from — the package, the
# lockfile, the tsconfigs and `src2` — so `ios/` and `android/` are left out by
# not being named at all. `src2` travels whole, though, and `export-ignore` is
# what keeps the parts of it only a Mac has any use for off the droplet.
#
# The **packages** they need are a different question and cannot be solved
# here: `deploy.sh` runs a plain `npm ci`, and it has to, because the server
# starts through `sucrase` from `devDependencies`. So the native packages do
# install on the droplet. See `src2/MOBILE.md` for what that costs.
src2/maestro   export-ignore
src2/tools     export-ignore
